% =============================================================================
% will sequent rules — the ∃_ρ fragment (TODO_0298 item 1; THY_0027)
% =============================================================================
%
% will's backward judgment = gill.rules (loaded FIRST — calculus.load takes
% a rules-file list; the shared fragment is inherited by reference, never
% copied) plus the will-OWN rules below: the weight-graded existential by
% draw-token internalization (THY_0027 §2). Rule NAMES encode the mechanical
% key (connective_side — the kernel and the prover derive the principal's
% tag and side from the name); @pretty carries the proof-theoretic reading:
%
%   drawn_l      ∃_ρ-R(c) — consume the token, witness the existential
%   drawn_l2     ghost     — weakening restricted to the token class
%   superpose_l  ∃-L       — the standard eigenvariable rule
%   draw         @draw     — one collapse event as a checked step (oracle,
%                            checker-bound like @fire; not enumerated in
%                            search — no principal, keyed by name)
%
% Weight is a FUNCTION OF THE ENDSEQUENT: w = Π ρ(c) over the drawn
% hypotheses present (THY_0027 §1) — no rule below carries a weight; the
% priors live in program data (`@w`, materialized as `prior s c ρ` facts)
% and are consulted only by the @draw checker and boundary readers.

@formulas A, B, C

% ∃_ρ-R (THY_0027 §2), implemented as a left rule on the token: given
% that a draw of C at sort S occurred, assert the superposed existential
% via C. The premise opens the binder body with the TOKEN'S member
% (@binding witness C — template binder opening, rule-interpreter); the
% succedent pattern forces token sort = wave sort. Non-invertible:
% choosing which token to spend commits the witness. Rung-2 note: the
% rule substitutes C as given, so a structured witness needs a ground
% member term in the token — lazy head-only tokens are the @draw/driver
% discipline, iterated ∃_ρ is its sequent reading (THY_0027 §8).
drawn_l: G ; D, drawn C S |- superpose S (exists X. A)
  <- G ; D |- A
  @side l
  @template true
  @binding witness C
  @pretty "∃ρR"
  @invertible false.

% ghost (trace weakening, THY_0027 §2/§5): tokens are affine — Δ proper
% stays linear. Forced by closure under cut reduction (§3a); excluded
% from the canonical counting class exactly like ordinary weakening
% under focusing. Non-invertible: discarding a token loses a ∃_ρ-R.
% @affine lets the prover insert this rule at the search boundaries
% (root leftovers, additive-branch balancing — §3h's "a branch that
% draws less discharges the surplus by ghost") where committed premise
% search cannot decide token consumption locally.
drawn_l2: G ; D, drawn C S |- B
  <- G ; D |- B
  @pretty "ghost"
  @affine true
  @invertible false.

% ∃-L (THY_0027 §2): the standard eigenvariable rule, token-neutral.
superpose_l: G ; D, superpose S (exists X. A) |- B
  <- G ; D, A |- B
  @template true
  @binding eigenvariable
  @pretty "∃ρL".

% Plain ∃ (token-free — THY_0027 §4's erasure target, in will's binder
% syntax; ill.rules' exists_r/exists_l with the binder made explicit).
% Operationally this is the M1 SKOLEM: the driver opens a plain ∃ with an
% evar it never collapses — exists_l is that opening's sequent reading.
exists_r: G ; D |- exists X. A
  <- G ; D |- A
  @template true
  @binding metavar
  @pretty "∃R"
  @invertible false.

exists_l: G ; D, exists X. A |- B
  <- G ; D, A |- B
  @template true
  @binding eigenvariable
  @pretty "∃L".

% @draw (TODO_0298 item 1b): one collapse event as a first-class step —
% consume the wave fact and one matching token, produce the body opened
% with the drawn witness. The witness record and its verification against
% the program's sort system and declared priors live in the config-bound
% checker (lib/prover/draw-check.js — calculus.stepCheckers via kit.js);
% the kernel stays draw-blind (P1 slot routing). The step is DERIVABLE
% (cut of drawn_l against superpose_l — THY_0026 §5: collapse is a
% principal cut; the minted token is the record the reduct keeps).
draw: G ; D |- C
  @pretty "@draw"
  @invertible false.
